261
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,020
He called me Captain Crane.

262
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:44,700
How do you know him?

263
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,380
I won't give you no trouble.

264
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:48,760
I swear I won't.

265
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,059
Just don't.

266
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,060
Don't let them take me.

267
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,300
Leave her be.

268
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:55,980
But she recognized the ring. She knew it
was Captain Crane's.

269
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,100
She looked me right in the eye like she
knew me.

270
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:04,050
You're him.

271
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:06,770
Ezekiel Crane.

272
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,230
Really, men can't see past their noses.

273
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,150
It's very simple.

274
00:19:13,090 --> 00:19:16,670
Captain Crane lived a sailor's life. He
stopped in a thousand ports, met a

275
00:19:16,670 --> 00:19:17,670
thousand women.

276
00:19:17,950 --> 00:19:20,070
We have no right to bother this poor
woman.

277
00:19:20,370 --> 00:19:21,510
Let's just leave her alone.

278
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:23,630
Here?

279
00:19:24,210 --> 00:19:25,370
In a place like this?

280
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:26,950
What else can we do?

281
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:29,590
This is where she lives.

282
00:19:30,630 --> 00:19:32,070
Besides, we don't even know her name.

283
00:19:33,350 --> 00:19:34,910
She'll cut your death in a night like
that.

284
00:19:35,830 --> 00:19:36,950
It's going to pour for sure.

285
00:19:38,870 --> 00:19:40,130
Let's take her back to your place.

286
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:41,550
My place?

287
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:43,050
I can't do that.

288
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,110
Take her to the angels.

289
00:19:45,550 --> 00:19:48,070
I can't. I'm just staying there until I
find a room of my own.

290
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,170
Besides, they'd never understand.

291
00:19:50,630 --> 00:19:52,170
I see. They won't understand.

292
00:19:52,630 --> 00:19:55,050
But I'm supposed to take a perfect
stranger back to my room.

293
00:19:55,670 --> 00:19:58,090
If she's a friend of Captain Crane,
she's no stranger.

294
00:19:59,890 --> 00:20:01,450
I got this feeling, Felicity.

295
00:20:02,450 --> 00:20:04,430
Something tells me we're doing wrong if
we leave her here.

296
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:48,340
I've never seen neither of them ever
again!

297
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,180
Are you asleep yet?

298
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:17,940
Yes.

299
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,680
I'm not.

300
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,420
Well, thank you for telling me.

301
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,160
Sorry.

302
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:26,580
Night.

303
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:34,740
Felicity?

304
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,960
What?

305
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:37,960
She's sleeping like a baby.

306
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:41,560
Everybody in Halifax is sleeping like a
baby, Gus.

307
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,480
Except for you and I.

308
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:49,500
Look, I'm sorry I can't stay up all
night and talk. I've just got such a

309
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:50,500
day ahead of me tomorrow.

310
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,240
I think it's best if we just think of
night.

311
00:21:54,660 --> 00:21:55,660
Night.

312
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:06,480
Gus?

313
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,720
Gee, Felicity.

314
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:11,120
How's a fella supposed to sleep if you
keep pestering him?

315
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:14,660
Why are you going to so much trouble for
someone you just bumped into?

316
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:21,840
Most of my life, kind of like a big
empty hole,

317
00:22:22,060 --> 00:22:25,180
never knowing who I am or where I come
from.

318
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:29,340
You're Felicity King. You're from
Avonlea.

319
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,100
You know your mother and father, your
whole family.

320
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:40,040
Me, I don't know nothing but myself,
except a few things I can't

321
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:43,340
forget, like my mother's gravestone.

322
00:22:45,110 --> 00:22:48,290
Eliza Pike, born 1863, died 1894.

323
00:22:51,050 --> 00:22:53,270
Then there's Abe Pike, the pa.

324
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:56,410
He's nothing to brag about.

325
00:23:00,450 --> 00:23:01,450
What is it?

326
00:23:03,210 --> 00:23:05,710
Do you think there's something that this
woman might know?

327
00:23:06,910 --> 00:23:07,910
I'm not sure.

328
00:23:09,390 --> 00:23:11,890
She's gnawing away at me, though,
thinking about things.

329
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:16,700
Maybe I should stop dragging up what's
best for God.

330
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:21,560
And I say to myself, no, keep digging,
get to the bottom of it.

331
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:24,620
Difficult to put the path to where it
belongs.

332
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,560
Look at you and me.

333
00:23:28,620 --> 00:23:29,880
Do we belong to the past?

334
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:33,120
You're a part of me, Felicity.

335
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:35,520
I don't have no past.

336
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:39,040
Meeting you and your family was when my
life started.

337
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:40,760
What can I do, Gus?

338
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:42,980
Do you want me to help you?

339
00:23:44,110 --> 00:23:45,790
I'm not pushing you anymore, Felicity.

340
00:23:46,970 --> 00:23:49,330
I'm just asking you to stick with me a
while longer.

341
00:23:50,890 --> 00:23:52,870
Until I figure out what's going on here.

342
00:23:56,890 --> 00:24:02,350
It's like... When you smell the sea and
you hear the wind howling.

343
00:24:03,310 --> 00:24:04,690
The sky's still clear.

344
00:24:06,370 --> 00:24:08,630
What you know on your bones, a storm's
brewing.

345
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:12,050
It's like that.

346
00:24:16,330 --> 00:24:17,510
We're on to something, you and me.

347
00:24:20,070 --> 00:24:21,070
Don't ask me why.

348
00:24:22,950 --> 00:24:23,950
I just know it.

349
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:41,110
There.

350
00:24:42,010 --> 00:24:43,270
You're looking all prettied up.

351
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:47,270
Would you like some more tea?

352
00:24:52,070 --> 00:24:54,910
It was a present from Captain Crane.

353
00:24:55,650 --> 00:24:56,930
Gave it to me before he left.

354
00:24:59,190 --> 00:25:00,690
Sail the seven seas, Captain.

355
00:25:02,330 --> 00:25:03,330
I won't know.

356
00:25:04,250 --> 00:25:05,250
I won't tell.

357
00:25:06,590 --> 00:25:11,650
Look, I know what you think, but I'm not
Ezekiel Crane.

358
00:25:12,710 --> 00:25:14,750
The ring with his, you got that part
right.

359
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:16,920
But I'm not him.

360
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:20,100
How do you do?

361
00:25:21,140 --> 00:25:22,440
My name's Gus Pike.

362
00:25:28,380 --> 00:25:29,820
I'm only trying to make friends.

363
00:25:32,220 --> 00:25:33,220
No.

364
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:35,140
No, they took him away.

365
00:25:35,540 --> 00:25:37,040
He's lost. He's lost.

366
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:38,960
Who's lost?

367
00:25:46,190 --> 00:25:47,490
Friends say, how do you do?

368
00:25:48,650 --> 00:25:50,650
My name's Gus Pike.

369
00:25:53,230 --> 00:25:54,330
What's yours?

370
00:25:59,030 --> 00:26:04,390
She's like the swallow that flies so
high

371
00:26:04,390 --> 00:26:09,350
Like the river that never runs dry

372
00:26:09,350 --> 00:26:13,270
She's like the sun...

373
00:26:27,340 --> 00:26:28,880
Am I crazy thinking what I'm thinking?

374
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:31,380
There could be a million Elizas.

375
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:33,480
It's a very common name.

376
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:36,000
That's true. I know it's true.

377
00:26:36,580 --> 00:26:40,940
But my mother's name was Eliza. Gosh,
she can't be your mother. You told me

378
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:42,180
your mother died years ago.

379
00:26:42,540 --> 00:26:47,140
Besides, we don't even know her last
name, and she's not about to tell us.

380
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:51,760
She's the right age, Felicity.

381
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:55,660
And her eyes...

382
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:58,840
Help my butter eyes.

383
00:27:03,620 --> 00:27:04,620
Can't be.

384
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:07,220
Can it?

385
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:08,640
You know it's impossible.

386
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:13,000
You came across someone with the same
name as your mother.

387
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:15,800
Call it fate, but that's all it is.

388
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,400
I don't think so.

389
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:20,780
That's not all it is.

390
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:23,440
Gus, you're letting your imagination run
away with you.

391
00:27:23,980 --> 00:27:25,100
Let's use common sense.

392
00:27:25,610 --> 00:27:28,430
Let's go to the police and turn her over
for safekeeping.

393
00:27:29,130 --> 00:27:30,130
The police?

394
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:37,430
No.

395
00:27:37,850 --> 00:27:38,970
I can't do that.

396
00:27:41,270 --> 00:27:42,810
All right, not the police.

397
00:27:44,890 --> 00:27:47,450
But there are places for people like
her, Gus.

398
00:27:47,850 --> 00:27:48,850
Nice places.

399
00:27:49,010 --> 00:27:50,030
I've read about them.

400
00:27:50,830 --> 00:27:51,830
We'll find one.

401
00:28:05,610 --> 00:28:06,610
look at you.

402
00:28:07,950 --> 00:28:10,350
She can't stay here. She's been here
before.

403
00:28:10,810 --> 00:28:13,250
You know her? She tries to run.

404
00:28:13,590 --> 00:28:16,390
We can't have that sort. It upsets the
others.

405
00:28:17,770 --> 00:28:20,270
What do you mean she tries to run? Did
she escape from here?

406
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:21,930
Oh, plenty of times.

407
00:28:22,650 --> 00:28:23,690
What's her last name?

408
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:27,290
They don't have last names. Not real
ones.

409
00:28:27,770 --> 00:28:29,070
They get put here.

410
00:28:29,330 --> 00:28:31,310
You mean somebody brought her here?

411
00:28:31,910 --> 00:28:32,910
Who?

412
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:36,680
You must keep records of such things. We
don't keep records.

413
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:40,160
They pay their money, we don't ask
questions.

414
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:41,920
Now, come on now.

415
00:28:43,260 --> 00:28:45,220
I wouldn't leave a dog in a place like
this.

416
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:55,800
If there's a chance back in Avonlea,
even a small one, I need to know.

417
00:28:56,260 --> 00:28:58,320
Gus, it's such a wild idea.

418
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:01,600
I hope you'll stick with me for
yesterday.

419
00:29:02,870 --> 00:29:03,870
You know I will.

420
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:42,560
Daniel King, if you don't stop eating
those, you're going to have a very sore

421
00:29:42,560 --> 00:29:43,560
tummy tonight.

422
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:46,100
Janet, make sure you core those
properly.

423
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:47,520
Yes, Henry.

424
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:51,340
Daniel, you leave those apples alone. I
didn't get them just for you. Daniel.

425
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:54,800
Oh, Felicity.

426
00:29:58,420 --> 00:29:59,420
Oh, Gus.

427
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:02,880
Gus Pike, is this really you?

428
00:30:03,140 --> 00:30:04,200
It's great to see you, Miss King.

429
00:30:05,020 --> 00:30:07,220
Felicity. Why are you home from school?

430
00:30:07,500 --> 00:30:10,160
What's wrong? Are you sick? Mother,
mother, please don't get excited. I'll

431
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,160
explain everything later.

432
00:30:11,380 --> 00:30:14,720
Sorry to bother you like this, Miss
King, but I have something important I

433
00:30:14,720 --> 00:30:15,720
to talk to you about.

434
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:18,220
You and Felicity.

435
00:30:19,620 --> 00:30:23,580
Felicity, what is wrong? I demand to
know why you're at home from school

436
00:30:23,580 --> 00:30:24,580
now.

437
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:32,800
Mother, Aunt Hedy, we brought someone
with us.

438
00:30:36,590 --> 00:30:37,590
This is Eliza.

439
00:30:51,650 --> 00:30:58,170
I don't believe I caught your last name.

440
00:30:59,630 --> 00:31:02,610
She hasn't got one, Mrs. King.

441
00:31:05,250 --> 00:31:08,890
Felicity, dear, give me a hand with
these dishes, will you?

442
00:31:10,150 --> 00:31:11,150
Excuse me.

443
00:31:18,290 --> 00:31:22,050
Felicity, dear, before I make an article
of myself, who is this person?

444
00:31:23,970 --> 00:31:26,630
Daddy, it's going to be difficult to
understand.

445
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:47,130
Gus. I'm not disturbing you, am I?

446
00:31:50,350 --> 00:31:51,990
I've made us some hot chocolate.

447
00:31:52,730 --> 00:31:54,890
Good. I'm glad you're still up.

448
00:31:57,590 --> 00:31:58,910
Got a lot on my mind.

449
00:32:02,410 --> 00:32:04,590
It took me a while to quiet her down.

450
00:32:06,730 --> 00:32:07,730
Dear me.

451
00:32:08,870 --> 00:32:11,750
It looks like you got yourself in a fine
mess this time.

452
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:15,160
You think I did wrong bringing Eliza
here?

453
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:18,880
Well, I... Oh, no.

454
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:20,740
No, dear boy.

455
00:32:21,980 --> 00:32:23,560
Heaven is where your home is.

456
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:26,080
Home is where you go when you're in
trouble.

457
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:32,140
You do seem to attract trouble in
inordinately large doses.

458
00:32:33,540 --> 00:32:36,820
I hope you're not doubting me, Miss
Kang.

459
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:40,600
I have never doubted you, Gaspite.

460
00:32:42,320 --> 00:32:44,260
Not from the minute I first met you.

461
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:51,020
Though I swear I've never met a soul
more determined than you are.

462
00:32:53,060 --> 00:32:54,460
That's what Felicity says.

463
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:57,120
It is still Felicity, then.

464
00:32:58,380 --> 00:32:59,380
Always was.

465
00:33:01,700 --> 00:33:03,000
I'll tell you this, Miss King.

466
00:33:04,380 --> 00:33:06,200
She's there for me when I'm in a jam.

467
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:12,200
Love's something more than merely
pulling one another out of jams, you

468
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:17,520
What's she to do if... if school refuses
to take her back?

469
00:33:17,980 --> 00:33:18,980
I don't know.

470
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:20,660
And I'm worried about that.

471
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:25,400
I want her dreams to come true, Miss
King, and I don't want to wreck them for

472
00:33:25,400 --> 00:33:26,400
her.

473
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:31,980
Perhaps you are her dream, Gaspik.

474
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:35,700
I wish I was.

475
00:33:38,640 --> 00:33:40,180
I wish a whole lot of things.

476
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:47,280
Miss King, about Eliza.

477
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:51,080
Do you think I'm chasing a ghost or
what?

478
00:33:53,780 --> 00:33:56,240
Far as we know, your mother is dead,
boy.

479
00:33:58,040 --> 00:34:04,320
Terrible as that is. Surely you must try
to put all that behind you and get on

480
00:34:04,320 --> 00:34:05,320
with your life.

481
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:06,880
I can't.

482
00:34:09,020 --> 00:34:11,659
I can't get past it no matter how hard I
try.

483
00:34:19,949 --> 00:34:21,530
Did you ever hear talk from anyone?

484
00:34:22,350 --> 00:34:23,750
About my mother, I mean.

485
00:34:26,010 --> 00:34:27,650
It's of course about us both.

486
00:34:28,530 --> 00:34:29,949
It was ages ago.

487
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:32,590
Can you remember what it was? I need to
know.

488
00:34:33,770 --> 00:34:34,770
Let me see.

489
00:34:35,710 --> 00:34:37,449
Oh, yes.

490
00:34:38,889 --> 00:34:42,510
Some hearsay of Rachel Lynn's, if I
recall.

491
00:34:43,850 --> 00:34:48,810
Something about Abe Pike's wife, your
mother, coming from a farm.

492
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:54,110
Out past Pat Fruin's place. Pat Fruin,
you say?

493
00:35:11,270 --> 00:35:12,610
I've been here before.

494
00:35:14,570 --> 00:35:15,870
I don't know when.

495
00:35:22,060 --> 00:35:23,100
She remembers something.

496
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:31,500
Do you want to go up there?

497
00:35:32,360 --> 00:35:33,360
No.

498
00:35:33,940 --> 00:35:34,940
No.

499
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:36,140
There's another way.

500
00:35:58,380 --> 00:35:59,380
It's no use.

501
00:36:00,980 --> 00:36:01,980
No, no.

502
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:11,800
You've

503
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:21,160
done

504
00:36:21,160 --> 00:36:22,160
all you could.

505
00:36:23,600 --> 00:36:24,700
No, I didn't.

506
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:27,300
What?

507
00:36:28,759 --> 00:36:30,020
There's still a grave.

508
00:36:30,520 --> 00:36:31,700
Oh, God, no.

509
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:34,240
I have to see if she's buried there.

510
00:36:34,820 --> 00:36:36,020
You can't do it.

511
00:36:37,720 --> 00:36:39,220
That's all I got left, Felicity.

512
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:55,380
Please hurry up. If anyone finds us
here, we're going to be... Come on,

513
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:56,420
Felicity, don't be so scared.

514
00:36:57,080 --> 00:36:58,260
Felix King, I'm not afraid.

515
00:36:59,140 --> 00:37:01,120
Well, Gus, it's your mother.

516
00:37:01,640 --> 00:37:02,640
You open it up.

517
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:32,860
Nothing but a pile of mud.

518
00:37:38,340 --> 00:37:43,240
And think of desecrating a grave as a
serious crime.

519
00:37:43,700 --> 00:37:50,660
I realize this is important to you, but
in my opinion, you have to abandon this

520
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:51,660
search. You understand?

521
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:53,740
But the coffin was empty.

522
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,600
Doesn't that prove anything?

523
00:37:56,060 --> 00:37:58,880
That doesn't mean that that woman in the
kitchen is your mother.

524
00:37:59,180 --> 00:38:00,720
But it's possible, isn't it?

525
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:02,000
It's true, Mother.

526
00:38:02,660 --> 00:38:03,760
Maybe it wasn't before.

527
00:38:04,260 --> 00:38:07,160
But you have to admit that now there is
a possibility.

528
00:38:08,180 --> 00:38:09,180
Isn't there, Felix?

529
00:38:09,300 --> 00:38:10,300
Oh, yeah, sure.

530
00:38:10,340 --> 00:38:11,680
Anything else you want to dig up, Gus?

531
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:14,300
She knows this ring.

532
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:16,040
She knows Captain Crane.

533
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:20,260
I don't care if it sounds crazy. I'm
looking after her. Please don't do this

534
00:38:20,260 --> 00:38:21,260
yourself.

535
00:38:21,700 --> 00:38:23,800
What you want to be real just isn't.

536
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:25,120
She's nobody, Gus.

537
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:28,000
She's just a vagrant you found on a city
street.

538
00:38:28,750 --> 00:38:32,590
Oh, you persist in this, you'll wind up
wandering around with her for the rest

539
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:33,590
of your life.

540
00:38:33,690 --> 00:38:35,410
Faith up to the truth, Gus Pike.

541
00:38:35,750 --> 00:38:37,990
That woman will be nothing but a burden
to you.

542
00:38:47,670 --> 00:38:51,230
I can't imagine what it was like for you
as a child.

543
00:39:01,210 --> 00:39:03,810
upstairs. Daniel, where did she go?

544
00:39:04,130 --> 00:39:05,130
He doesn't know.

545
00:39:06,210 --> 00:39:07,210
I'll take the woods.

546
00:39:07,830 --> 00:39:09,110
I'll look around the house.

547
00:39:09,550 --> 00:39:10,630
Felix, come with me.

548
00:39:11,790 --> 00:39:12,790
Eliza?

549
00:39:15,130 --> 00:39:16,130
Eliza!

550
00:39:17,010 --> 00:39:19,430
The devil's pulpit!

551
00:40:15,600 --> 00:40:16,600
It ain't a plank.

552
00:40:24,340 --> 00:40:25,340
It's true.

553
00:40:30,580 --> 00:40:31,920
Everything I thought...

554
00:40:49,040 --> 00:40:50,040
Captain Crane.

555
00:40:53,080 --> 00:40:54,320
To Eliza.

556
00:40:55,160 --> 00:40:56,920
My own true love.

557
00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:01,560
You've got to tell me.

558
00:41:03,060 --> 00:41:05,320
Why was this buried under the devil's
pulpit?

559
00:41:06,820 --> 00:41:09,560
I can't go on knowing only bits and
pieces.

560
00:41:13,120 --> 00:41:14,280
You married Abe.

561
00:41:17,390 --> 00:41:18,490
with the Captain Crane you loved.

562
00:41:23,770 --> 00:41:24,770
Captain Crane.

563
00:41:27,970 --> 00:41:28,970
Isn't he my pa?

564
00:41:36,650 --> 00:41:37,830
What about Abe Pike?

565
00:41:40,530 --> 00:41:41,690
What about Abe Pike?

566
00:41:42,890 --> 00:41:43,890
Did he know?

567
00:41:47,580 --> 00:41:51,740
You've got to remember what happened.

568
00:41:54,080 --> 00:41:56,900
Did Abe Pike bury the coffin and tell
everyone you were dead?

569
00:41:58,080 --> 00:41:59,760
Was it Abe putting you in asylum?

570
00:42:03,880 --> 00:42:04,360
He

571
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:15,020
wrecked

572
00:42:15,020 --> 00:42:16,020
your life.

573
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:19,800
And mine too.

574
00:42:24,620 --> 00:42:25,860
There's my boy.

575
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:30,800
There's my little boy.

576
00:42:50,190 --> 00:42:51,190
What do you want me to do?

577
00:42:55,790 --> 00:42:57,230
I'll do anything you want.

578
00:43:14,730 --> 00:43:18,150
I have to take Eliza and find Captain
Crane, even if he's in Jamaica.

579
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:20,420
If anyone knows the truth about us, he
does.

580
00:43:23,220 --> 00:43:24,220
We're off.

581
00:43:27,840 --> 00:43:28,840
Goodbye.

582
00:43:29,980 --> 00:43:30,980
Yes, it is.

583
00:43:32,500 --> 00:43:33,920
Soon you'll marry me, Felicity.

584
00:43:35,600 --> 00:43:37,560
Don't let me go without a promise this
time.

585
00:43:38,080 --> 00:43:39,080
Say you'll be mine.

586
00:43:41,140 --> 00:43:42,600
I've always been yours, Gus.

587
00:43:44,360 --> 00:43:45,440
I'll be yours forever.

